WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:01.473
- [Narrator] When you think of snacks

00:00:01.473 --> 00:00:03.920
at a ballgame, you think hot dogs,

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.891
Cracker Jacks, peanuts, pretzels,

00:00:06.891 --> 00:00:09.308
and, of course, grasshoppers.

00:00:10.232 --> 00:00:12.320
Okay, maybe you don't, but the

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.251
Seattle Mariners and their fans sure do.

00:00:16.251 --> 00:00:18.918
(playful music)

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.101
So, how did this crunchy critter

00:00:24.101 --> 00:00:25.411
get a spot next to your everyday

00:00:25.411 --> 00:00:28.051
concession snacks at Safeco field?

00:00:28.051 --> 00:00:31.782
It all starts at this
restaurant with this guy.

00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:33.179
- My name's Manny Arce.

00:00:33.179 --> 00:00:35.411
I'm the executive chef here at Poquito's.

00:00:35.411 --> 00:00:37.562
The grasshoppers are grasshoppers.

00:00:37.562 --> 00:00:40.019
You know, they're a delicacy, but
they're also a snack.

00:00:40.019 --> 00:00:42.337
I put them on the menu here as a novelty

00:00:42.337 --> 00:00:45.496
when we opened, and we kind of just,
it's been on the menu

00:00:45.496 --> 00:00:47.429
for almost six and a half years.

00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:51.035
I describe them, crunchy
like a sunflower seed,

00:00:51.035 --> 00:00:53.570
um, salty, a little bit spicy.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:54.776
Uh, every once in a while, you get one

00:00:54.776 --> 00:00:57.176
that's a little squishier than you'd like.

00:00:57.176 --> 00:00:58.827
We just toast them and then we put salt

00:00:58.827 --> 00:01:01.205
and some lime and some chili on them.

00:01:01.205 --> 00:01:02.573
That's about all that we do to them.

00:01:02.573 --> 00:01:03.440
- [Narrator] It's one thing to see

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.840
restaurant success, but
Manny's grasshoppers

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.139
became the highlight of
going to Mariners' games.

00:01:09.139 --> 00:01:10.562
- [Manny] When Mariners were saying that

00:01:10.562 --> 00:01:13.483
we'd be a fit for them, I sent some out.

00:01:13.483 --> 00:01:16.992
- [Narrator] The response was unreal.

00:01:16.992 --> 00:01:20.092
As in 300,000 plus grasshoppers sold.

00:01:20.092 --> 00:01:22.461
- [Manny] We were selling out, you know,
before even the first inning,

00:01:22.461 --> 00:01:24.368
and I started off with 50 pounds,

00:01:24.368 --> 00:01:28.400
thinking like, oh, this'll last us,
you know, a month or two.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.840
It lasted us one day.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.760
To date, we've probably gone through

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.263
about a thousand pounds.

00:01:34.263 --> 00:01:37.488
People want more than, you know, 
hot dogs and popcorn,

00:01:37.488 --> 00:01:39.789
and nobody else had been
doing it at the stadium,

00:01:39.789 --> 00:01:40.755
so it's kind of one of these things

00:01:40.755 --> 00:01:43.090
that I think people
just really latched onto

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:47.090
and the popularity far
exceeded my expectations.

